date,os,session,session_name,session_id,method,check_required,host,mux,config,note
日期,作業系統,session,Claude session 名稱,session 識別碼,送達方式,需要檢查,主機,multiplexer,設定檔,備註
2026-09-09,macos,Swift-Cross-UI-Mac,Swift-Cross-UI-Mac,6c91a77a-086e-49d5-ad35-2d615900505e,session-id,no,local,screen,,"This Mac. session_id is this very session (its transcript is ~/.claude/projects/-Volumes-Windows-proj-Win-swift-cross-ui/6c91a77a-....jsonl). **A session-id beat is not the same act as a mux beat, and the difference is worth knowing before arming it**: claude -p -r <id> appends a HEADLESS turn to that conversation and returns the reply to this script, whereas the mux route types into a live terminal where a human can see it. Measured 2026-09-09 on a throwaway session: claude -p -r <id> ""Are you still working ?"" returned the same session_id and the reply Yes, I am here and ready to help"
2026-09-09,windows,Swift-Cross-UI-Windows,Swift-Cross-UI-Windows,(pending -- Windows will supply it),session-id,no,winnode,tmux,~/.multissh/generated/config2Win,"Windows-native claude, reached with multissh exec and claude -p -r <session_id>. **No multiplexer is involved on this route and none is needed**, which matters because the Windows side has no tmux, no screen and no pacman to install either. Measured 2026-09-09 through multissh -F config2Win winnode: claude is at /c/Users/lowei/AppData/Local/Microsoft/WinGet/Links/claude and reports 2.1.216. The session_id is what Windows supplies; until it does, this row stays check_required=no because a beat with no id has nothing to resume"
